      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a9fe9983955314156acc4f7|full_name}: I understand the problem with drawcalls. I was hoping to disable all drawcalls and simply have the wireframe of an avatar without any materials. Just like in a game engine's wireframe view, I was hoping just having the wireframe alone would be a good idea to see what an avatar's shape/silhouette is and what actions they are performing while not having to worry about frame rate. If this can be done as I think it could in theory, perhaps this could be a second alternative or player preference to hiding avatars.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-06-27T02:14:04.095Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I came up with an idea that to instead of using “hide all avatars”, use a wireframe of a player’s avatar so that you can see what they are doing while also having the ability to maintain a functional frame rate.",
